\begin{abstract}
We study pseudo-Dirac pairs of two almost mass-degenerate sterile Majorana neutrinos which generate light neutrino masses via a low-scale seesaw mechanism.
These pseudo-Dirac heavy neutral leptons can oscillate between interaction eigenstates that couple to leptons and antileptons and thus generate oscillations between lepton number conserving and lepton number violating processes.
With the \pSPSS, we introduce a minimal framework capable of describing the dominant features of low-scale seesaws at colliders and present a \software{FeynRules} implementation usable in Monte Carlo generators.
Additionally, we extend \software{MadGraph} to simulate heavy neutrino-antineutrino oscillations and present results from such simulations.
\end{abstract}


